    "ingredients": {
      "type": "zeta-ingredients",
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "tile",
          "settings": {
            "featured": false,
            "icon": "<svg viewbox=\"0 0 60 60\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polygon points=\"30,3 55,17 55,43 30,57 5,43 5,17\" stroke=\"#006E73\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"></polygon><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"30\" r=\"5\" stroke=\"#006E73\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"></circle><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"19\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#006E73\" opacity=\"0.4\"></circle><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"36\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#006E73\" opacity=\"0.4\"></circle><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"36\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#006E73\" opacity=\"0.4\"></circle></svg>",
            "tag": "",
            "corner_tag": "Most Studied",
            "label": "The Proven Anchor",
            "label_color": "teal",
            "name": "B. lactis HN019®",
            "source": "HOWARU™ certified · most-studied strain in the formula",
            "body": "<p>The anchor of this formula. In a randomized controlled trial of 100 adults, daily HN019® supplementation significantly reduced whole-gut transit time within 14 days — at both high and low doses. It adheres to epithelial cells, survives GI transit intact, and has a safety record spanning decades of published human research. The foundation every other strain is built around.</p>",
            "nick": ""
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "tile",
          "settings": {
            "featured": false,
            "icon": "<svg viewbox=\"0 0 60 60\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polygon points=\"30,3 57,30 30,57 3,30\" stroke=\"#B89968\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"></polygon><polygon points=\"30,15 45,30 30,45 15,30\" stroke=\"#B89968\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"></polygon><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"30\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#B89968\"></circle></svg>",
            "tag": "",
            "corner_tag": "",
            "label": "The Human Native",
            "label_color": "bronze",
            "name": "L. acidophilus La-14",
            "source": "of human origin · type A1 L. acidophilus",
            "body": "<p>Found naturally in the human intestinal tract, mouth, and vagina — and in fermented milks like kefir for centuries. The La-14 strain is of human origin, which matters: strains that evolved alongside human biology tend to adhere better and colonize more effectively. Demonstrates excellent adhesion to human epithelial cell lines. It belongs here.</p>",
            "nick": ""
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "tile",
          "settings": {
            "featured": false,
            "icon": "<svg viewbox=\"0 0 60 60\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M30 8 C30 8, 14 20, 14 34 C14 44 21 52 30 52 C39 52 46 44 46 34 C46 20 30 8 30 8Z\" stroke=\"#6B7280\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"></path><path d=\"M30 20 C30 20, 20 28, 20 36 C20 42 24 48 30 48\" stroke=\"#6B7280\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\" fill=\"none\"></path><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"30\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#6B7280\" opacity=\"0.5\"></circle></svg>",
            "tag": "",
            "corner_tag": "",
            "label": "The Fermented Foods Strain",
            "label_color": "mid",
            "name": "L. plantarum Lp-115",
            "source": "from plant origin · olives, sauerkraut, kimchi",
            "body": "<p>Found in lactic acid-fermented foods across cultures — olives, sauerkraut, kimchi — for centuries before we understood why. The Lp-115 strain is tough in the right way: resistant to low pH conditions, bile-tolerant at duodenal concentrations, and demonstrates excellent adhesion to epithelial cell lines. It doesn't just survive the GI tract. It's built for it.</p>",
            "nick": ""
          }
        },
        "i4": {
          "type": "tile",
          "settings": {
            "featured": false,
            "icon": "<svg viewbox=\"0 0 60 60\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"20\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" stroke=\"#8B7355\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"></rect><rect x=\"18\" y=\"25\" width=\"24\" height=\"10\" rx=\"5\" stroke=\"#8B7355\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"></rect><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"30\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#8B7355\" opacity=\"0.5\"></circle><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"30\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#8B7355\" opacity=\"0.3\"></circle><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"30\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#8B7355\" opacity=\"0.3\"></circle></svg>",
            "tag": "",
            "corner_tag": "",
            "label": "The Intestinal Specialist",
            "label_color": "sand",
            "name": "B. longum Bl-05",
            "source": "Bl-05 strain · intestinal environment native",
            "body": "<p>Well-suited to the intestinal environment — which sounds simple, but it's not. B. longum Bl-05 is resistant to both low pH and bile salts, meaning it makes it to the target tissue alive and ready. Well-established safety profile, documented performance in the gut. The quiet, reliable fourth member of this stack.</p>",
            "nick": ""
          }
        }
      },
